@startuml
!include style.puml

title PWasm MultiTxnWal Recovery States
caption Wizard Engine commit 8b262f4c24497bd2c5abe37c4b84c40dd4a97bf8, 2026-07-02.
caption MultiTxnWal.recover(); replay floor = durableAppliedSeq (loaded from newest-generation WalSuperblock).

[*] --> LoadSuperblock : mount()

state "Load superblock" as LoadSuperblock
LoadSuperblock : loadSuperblock() picks the valid copy
LoadSuperblock : with the higher generation
LoadSuperblock : -> durableAppliedSeq, logEpoch
LoadSuperblock --> ScanRing : openOk
LoadSuperblock --> Failed : corrupt / !openOk

state "Scan ring" as ScanRing
ScanRing : scanCommittedRecords() walks the ring
ScanRing : validateRecord() keeps only records with
ScanRing : good magic/version/size, matching logEpoch,
ScanRing : valid entry widths, and a good FNV checksum
ScanRing --> SelectPrefix

state "Select contiguous prefix" as SelectPrefix
SelectPrefix : selectContiguousPrefix(candidates)
SelectPrefix : takes the run whose txnSeq is contiguous
SelectPrefix : from durableAppliedSeq + 1
SelectPrefix --> Redo : selected not empty
SelectPrefix --> GapAbandon : empty but candidates exist\n(sequence gap)
SelectPrefix --> NothingToReplay : no candidates

state "Redo records" as Redo
Redo : for each selected record redoRecord()
Redo : (writeAfterImage of every LogEntry);
Redo : appliedSeqVolatile advances per record
Redo --> PersistData

state "Persist replayed data" as PersistData
PersistData : backendRegion.persistChanges()
PersistData --> Failed : persist fails
PersistData --> PublishReplay : ok

state "Publish replay" as PublishReplay
PublishReplay : writeSuperblock(recoveredMaxSeq, logEpoch + 1)
PublishReplay : logEpoch++  (fences replayed records)
PublishReplay : durableAppliedSeq = recoveredMaxSeq
PublishReplay : reset headOffset / activeRecords
PublishReplay --> Recovered : superblock durable
PublishReplay --> Failed : superblock write fails

state "Gap-abandon" as GapAbandon
GapAbandon : valid records after a gap are NOT applied
GapAbandon : writeSuperblock(durableAppliedSeq, logEpoch + 1)
GapAbandon : logEpoch++ ; currentGeneration++
GapAbandon : reset volatile state
GapAbandon --> Clean

state "Nothing to replay" as NothingToReplay
NothingToReplay : nextTxnSeq = durableAppliedSeq + 1
NothingToReplay : appliedSeqVolatile = durableAppliedSeq
NothingToReplay : reset volatile state
NothingToReplay --> Clean

Recovered --> [*] : recover() = true
Clean --> [*] : recover() = false (no replay)
Failed --> [*] : recover() = false (aborted)

note right of PublishReplay
Epoch bump is the anti-double-apply guard:
after the new superblock is durable, the just-replayed
current-epoch records no longer match logEpoch, so a
later mount cannot re-apply them.
end note

@enduml
